---
term: Act of commission
aka:
  - Interventionist commission
section: life-cycle
order: 35
definition: The end of the formation gradient at which a [[parent corporation]] organizes a subsidiary charter to establish itself on a jurisdiction, and then grants it rights according to their mutual articles.
example: A national health corporation commissions a regional pandemic-preparedness corporation. The commission sets its budget, gives it jurisdiction over medical stockpiles, and schedules a review in five years.
seeAlso:
  - charter-formation
  - voluntary-admission
  - contract
---
Commission suits cases where a parent needs a dedicated body to pursue part of its own objective. The subsidiary holds a [[contract]] with the parent from its commission until [[admission]]. The opposite end is [[voluntary admission]].
